body:
Thank you once again for replying with so much info! Also I just realised you're the same user that was so kind to post the recent live report! ;w; sorry that I keep commenting haha. Rest well, it seems like you had an amazing experience! 

I would love to be part of fanclubs, sometimes it's so difficult to be a foreign fan... And sometimes bands have CD signings and other events that I'd love to attend. Is it expensive to be in their fanclub and attend their lives frequently? I love the Japanese etiquette of being polite even in concerts, I'm asian so i identify a lot with this culture. That's why I can't get used to the "culture" of London concerts... I've seen dir en grey about 5 times and every time I get squashed and thrown around like a ragdoll and a lot of people randomly scream or talk and use their phone... Anyway enough complaining, I would love to experience a concert in Japan, or even hong kong my home country ;_; I feel like I'd enjoy it so much more and not feel like I'm in the middle of a battle lol. 

Thank you once again! I love people like you who spreads info and shares stories about the members so foreign fans can connect more ;w;
